            <ArticleTitle>Unligated left internal mammary artery side branch resulting in coronary artery steal syndrome.</ArticleTitle>
            <Pagination>
                <MedlinePgn>487-90</MedlinePgn>
            </Pagination>
            <ELocationID EIdType="doi" ValidYN="Y">10.1111/j.1540-8191.2011.01297.x</ELocationID>
            <Abstract>
                <AbstractText>Whether internal mammary artery side branches have the potential for hemodynamically significant flow steal in cases of postcoronary surgery ischemia remains a controversial issue. We present a case in which coil embolization of two unligated side branches resulted in symptomatic improvement and resolution of ischemia as evidenced by myoview imaging. </AbstractText>
